NAME
       ping - send ICMP echo requests

SYNOPSIS
       ping [-c count] [-s size] <host>

DESCRIPTION
       Sends ICMP echo requests to HOST, which may be a name or an
       address, and prints each reply with its round-trip time. Runs
       until interrupted unless -c is given.

OPTIONS
       -c N   stop after N requests
       -s N   send N bytes of payload instead of 32. Anything past the
              link's limit is sent as IP fragments and reassembled by
              the far end, so this is the way to test that path.

SEE ALSO
       ifconfig(1), nslookup(1), nmap(1)
